11 0 obj
<< /Length 1500 >>
stream
BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 760 Td
(Apache Kafka & KRaft) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 730 Td
(The Ultimate Interview & Production Guide) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 700 Td
(1. Kafka brokers: servers that store and serve partitions and handle producer/consumer traffic.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 685 Td
(2. Topics and partitions: logical streams broken into ordered logs for parallelism and scalability.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 670 Td
(3. Producers: push records to leader partition, use keys, batching, and compression for throughput.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 655 Td
(4. Consumers: read from offsets and work in consumer groups to parallelize work safely.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 640 Td
(5. Consumer offsets: committed to __consumer_offsets to support restart and replay.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 625 Td
(6. ZooKeeper: older Kafka coordination layer for metadata, brokers, and controller election.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 610 Td
(7. KRaft: Kafka-native Raft metadata quorum without external ZooKeeper dependency.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 595 Td
(8. ISR: In-Sync Replicas that are fully caught up and eligible to become partition leaders.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 580 Td
(9. Data durability: replication factor, acks=all, and min.insync.replicas protect against loss.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
12 0 obj
<< /Length 1700 >>
stream
BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 760 Td
(ZooKeeper vs KRaft) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 730 Td
(ZooKeeper mode uses Zab consensus and a quorum of ensemble nodes.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 715 Td
(Leader election: nodes vote based on zxid and myid, and a quorum selects the leader.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 700 Td
(Kafka controller election: broker creates /controller and first write wins.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 685 Td
(Partition leader election: controller selects a leader from ISR when a leader fails.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 670 Td
(KRaft uses Raft protocol directly in Kafka metadata quorum.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 655 Td
(Leader election: followers time out, become candidates, and require majority quorum votes.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 640 Td
(Heartbeats: leader sends periodic heartbeats; if missing, followers trigger a new election.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 625 Td
(KRaft removes the external ZooKeeper dependency and simplifies operations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 610 Td
(Modern Kafka deployments prefer KRaft for metadata and failover control.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 585 Td
(Interview view: KRaft is faster, simpler, and more self-contained than ZooKeeper mode.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
13 0 obj
<< /Length 2200 >>
stream
BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 760 Td
(Interview Questions and Scenarios) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 730 Td
(Q: What is Kafka? A: Distributed event streaming platform for high-throughput, durable pipelines.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 715 Td
(Q: What is a consumer group? A: A set of consumers that share partition ownership.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 700 Td
(Q: What is an offset? A: The position of a message within a partition.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 685 Td
(Q: Why use Kafka? A: Decoupling, replayability, scalability, fault tolerance, and throughput.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 670 Td
(Scenario: Consumer lag rising rapidly. Action: scale consumers, add partitions, and monitor lag.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 655 Td
(Scenario: Broker fails. Action: use replication and ISR elections to maintain availability.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 640 Td
(Scenario: Data loss during writes. Action: verify acks=all, replication factor, and min.insync.replicas.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 625 Td
(Scenario: Duplicate processing. Action: use idempotent producers and dedupe logic in consumers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 610 Td
(Scenario: Consumer rebalance loops. Action: tune session.timeout.ms and max.poll.interval.ms.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 595 Td
(Scenario: Payment processing requires exactly-once semantics. Use Kafka transactions + read_committed.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 580 Td
(Production answer: Kafka provides at-least-once by default; exactly-once requires deliberate design.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
14 0 obj
<< /Length 2200 >>
stream
BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 760 Td
(Production Configs and Monitoring) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 730 Td
(Producer config: bootstrap.servers, acks=all, enable.idempotence=true, linger.ms=20, compression.type=zstd.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 715 Td
(Consumer config: group.id, auto.offset.reset=earliest, enable.auto.commit=false, max.poll.records=500.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 700 Td
(Topic config: num.partitions, replication.factor, min.insync.replicas, retention.ms, cleanup.policy.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 685 Td
(Do: use 3x replication, monitor lag, disk, and request latency in production.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 670 Td
(Dont: run single-broker production, ignore under-replicated partitions, or set acks=0 for critical topics.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 655 Td
(Metrics to monitor: underreplicated partitions, offline partitions, request queue time, lag, and GC pauses.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 640 Td
(Prometheus: scrape Kafka JMX exporter on port 7071 and visualize with Grafana.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 625 Td
(Example topic command: kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --create --topic prod.orders --partitions 6 --replication-factor 3) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 610 Td
(Example describe command: kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group payment-processor-service) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 595 Td
(Final summary: Kafka is built for durable, high-throughput, decoupled event streaming with modern KRaft leadership.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
